# Git checkpoints

At significant checkpoints — feature complete, deploy shipped, bug fixed and verified, or a clear stopping point — **commit and push to `origin`** without waiting to be asked.

- Follow the repo's existing commit-message style; prefer why over what.
- Do not commit `dist/`, secrets, or junk.
- Do not force-push `main`/`master`.
- If push fails (auth/network), report it; still leave the local commit.
- Skip trivial WIP thrash; batch related edits into one checkpoint when possible.
